  "nl_text": "The database name is rschema_0480 and it contains four tables: Property, Agent, User, and Responsibility. The Property table has the following columns: Address, Built_area, Construction_year, Is_apartment, Property_ID (primary key), Property_certificate, Property_photos, Sale_price, and Sales_status. The Agent table has the following columns: Agent_ID (primary key), Contact_number, Home_address, and Name. The User table has the following columns: Password, Role, User_ID (primary key), and Username. The Responsibility table has the following columns: Agent_ID (foreign key referencing Agent), Property_ID (foreign key referencing Property), Responsibility_end_time, Responsibility_start_time, and a composite primary key consisting of Agent_ID and Property_ID. The Responsibility table also has foreign key constraints referencing the Agent and Property tables, with update and delete rules of CASCADE and RESTRICT, respectively.",
  "gold_question": "This is a real estate information management system. For property management, the system records basic information for each property, including unique property ID, property certificate, address, construction year, built area, sale price, property photos and sales status (for sale, sold, off market), with additional apartment-specific information required for apartment-type properties. For real estate agent management, the system records basic information for each agent, including unique agent ID, name, home address and contact number. Each property can only be managed by one agent at a time, and the system needs to record the responsibility period (start time, end time). For user management, the system records basic information for each user, including unique user ID, username, password and role (real estate agent or system administrator). Users need to pass authentication before logging into the system. After logging in, real estate agents can enter information for properties they are responsible for selling, but this requires system administrator approval and authorization. All users can query property information, while system administrators can also export property information lists and periodically organize sales status, removing properties that are no longer for sale from the system.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0480.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0480\nCREATE TABLE `property` (\n  `property_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `built_area` float NOT NULL,\n  `construction_year` int(4) NOT NULL,\n  `is_apartment` tinyint(1) NOT NULL,\n  `property_certificate` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `property_photos` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `sale_price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `sales_status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`property_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `agent` (\n  `agent_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `contact_number` varchar(15) NOT NULL,\n  `home_address` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`agent_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `username` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `role` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `responsibility` (\n  `agent_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `property_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `responsibility_start_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `responsibility_end_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`agent_id`, `property_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `responsibility_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`agent_id`) REFERENCES `agent` (`agent_id`) ON DELETE RESTRICT ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `responsibility_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`property_id`) REFERENCES `property` (`property_id`) ON DELETE RESTRICT ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
